<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-3098] Livy Interpreter fails if row contains newline or tab</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-3098</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The Livy interpreter will return incorrect results if a row contains \n or \t characters.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In the case of the newline, the result will be:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Line is missing from results if the \n appears anywhere but the end of a cell&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;`String index out of range: 17` if it appears at the end of a cell&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;In the case of the tab, the result will be misaligned columns if the tab appears in the middle of a cell&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The output showing these error is attached.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment>&lt;p&gt;All environments&lt;/p&gt;</environment>
