&lt;p&gt;    The Livy interpreter will return incorrect results if a row contains \n or \t characters.&lt;br/&gt;
    In the case of the newline, the result will be:&lt;br/&gt;
    Line is missing from results if the \n appears anywhere but the end of a cell&lt;br/&gt;
    `String index out of range: 17` if it appears at the end of a cell&lt;br/&gt;
    In the case of the tab, the result will be misaligned columns if the tab appears in the middle of a cell&lt;br/&gt;
    The output showing these error is attached.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    I have changed the parsing and any newline or tab characters will be escaped&lt;/p&gt;

